<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuelan M-2 rises 0.38 pct in week to Jan 10.</title>
<headline>Venezuelan M-2 rises 0.38 pct in week to Jan 10.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan money supply, as measured by the monetary aggregate M-2, rose 0.38 percent or 20 billion bolivars to 5.283 trillion bolivars in the week to January 10, the central bank said.</p>
<p>At the beginning of 1997, M-2 was 5.357 trillion bolivars. At the beginning of 1996, M-2 was 3.548 trillion.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
</text>
